// The cathedral: its roof, the spire over the crossing, twin towers at the west front and two
// turrets at the apse, flying buttresses, stained glass within and without, the great door (three
// tiles wide) with the great rose in the gable over it and another rose above the throne, pillars,
// pews facing the throne, a crimson runner down the nave, candles and banners. Its floor is marble
// lozenges in bordered panels.
É = roof span=17,7 ridge=x top=9 pitch=3.5 tex=violet_slate wall=rough_stone on=C
Ê = cathedral_spire height=15 base=11 on=n
è = cathedral_tower height=15 shift=1,-1 on=C
é = cathedral_tower height=15 shift=1,1 on=C
ê = cathedral_tower height=10 width=2.2 helm=4 turret shift=0,-2 on=C
ë = cathedral_tower height=10 width=2.2 helm=4 turret shift=0,2 on=C
ï = cathedral_portal yaw=0 height=9 rose=10.6 on=n
